# Round 18, C1-1 (follows). L §4.3: "Write `at start_of(m)`, `at end_of(m) - 1 day` (m's last day, §4.2) or another
# day of m"; L §4.2: end_of(k) is "the first day after it". r_last reads March's law (v1, 100), r_next April's (v2,
# 200).
=== m.tally
model m
  tally 2
  on 2026-12-31
  start 2026-01-01
  end 2026-12-31
source s "s"
unit PLN: currency minor 0.01
input rate: money PLN
def r_last[m in months]: money PLN = rate at end_of(m) - 1 day
def r_next[m in months]: money PLN = rate at end_of(m)
version v1
  cite s
  governs 2026-01..2026-03
  known 2025-12-01
  rate = 100
version v2
  cite s
  governs 2026-04..
  known 2025-12-01
  rate = 200
ask q: r_last[2026-03], r_next[2026-03], end_of(2026-03)
=== expect
q: (100.00 PLN, 200.00 PLN, 2026-04-01)
  cut 2026-12-31
